# Privacy Policy — TabTidy

**Last updated: April 2026**

## Overview

TabTidy is a Chrome extension that groups your open tabs by domain. This policy explains how the extension handles your data.

## Data Collected

TabTidy stores the following data **locally in your browser only**:

- Saved sessions, including group names, colours, and the URLs of tabs within each group (up to 10 sessions)
- Your auto-group on startup preference

This data is used solely to provide the session save and restore feature.

## Data Storage

All data is stored using Chrome's `storage.local` API. It never leaves your browser and is not accessible to any website or third party.

Please note: saved sessions contain the URLs of tabs you choose to save. This data stays on your device and is never transmitted anywhere.

## Data Sharing

No data is collected, transmitted, or shared with any external server, service, or third party.

## Permissions

- **tabs** — used to read tab URLs and titles in order to group them by domain
- **tabGroups** — used to create, update, rename, and remove Chrome tab groups
- **storage** — used to save sessions and settings locally in your browser

## Changes to This Policy

This policy may be updated occasionally. The latest version will always be available at this URL.

